{"id":92,"date":"2026-07-09T14:25:53","date_gmt":"2026-07-09T14:25:53","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/localhost:8181\/historic-districts-fresh-air-ventilation-done-right-in-bethlehem\/"},"modified":"2026-07-15T20:44:31","modified_gmt":"2026-07-15T20:44:31","slug":"historic-districts-fresh-air-ventilation-done-right-in-bethlehem","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/historic-districts-fresh-air-ventilation-done-right-in-bethlehem\/","title":{"rendered":"You Sealed Your Bethlehem House Tight\u2014Now It Can&#8217;t Breathe"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text alignfull s-pencil-hero s-pencil-hero--split-industrial\" style=\"grid-template-columns:50% auto\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"697\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/10787664563_3d35f30f8e_b.jpg\" alt=\"brick rowhouse street\" class=\"wp-image-198\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/10787664563_3d35f30f8e_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/10787664563_3d35f30f8e_b-300x204.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/10787664563_3d35f30f8e_b-768x523.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;1501-1509 R Street NW&quot; by NCinDC, BY-ND, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<p class=\"s-pencil-hero__eyebrow wp-block-paragraph\">Bethlehem, PA \u00b7 HVAC Services<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading s-pencil-hero__title wp-block-heading\">When sealing stops the breathing<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"s-pencil-hero__lead wp-block-paragraph\">Seal a hundred-year-old house well enough and it stops breathing \u2014 the drafts you paid to eliminate were also the only fresh-air system it ever had.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-35f06ea7 wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"\/contact\/\">Book the Assessment<\/a><\/div>\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline is-style-outline--1\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"#content\">Explore Services<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"s-trust-bar\"><div class=\"s-trust__item\">15+ Years Serving PA<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Licensed &amp; Insured<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Same-Day Emergency<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Local to Your Area<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--sand has-tint-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text has-media-on-the-right\" style=\"grid-template-columns:auto 50%\"><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The air math that changed<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Bethlehem&#039;s historic blocks have been quietly weatherized one house at a time for two decades. Cellulose blown into balloon-framed walls, spray foam under rooflines, storm windows on stone buildings near the Monocacy Creek. Every project delivered: lower fuel bills, fewer drafts, less cycling. And nearly every one changed something nobody discussed \u2014 where the house gets its air. An old house was built to leak.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Occupants got fresh air through gaps around windows, rim joists, and chimneys. Close those paths and leftovers stay indoors: cooking odors that survive until breakfast, glass that sweats every January morning, closets developing musty edges, carbon dioxide levels in closed bedrooms rising to genuinely surprising readings. Air leakage is measured in air changes per hour at test pressure. An untouched circa-1900 Bethlehem house might test at twelve to fifteen;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">a thorough sealing job brings it down to five or six \u2014 below the point where random leakage reliably delivers fresh air that building science standards call for. Infiltration is weather-driven: a tightened house still gets outside air on a windy January night and almost none on calm fifty-five-degree afternoons, which is exactly when stuffiness complaints peak.<\/p>\n\n<\/div><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-thermostat-1-1024x683.png\" alt=\"thermostat - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1479\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-thermostat-1-1024x683.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-thermostat-1-300x200.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-thermostat-1-768x512.png 768w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-thermostat-1.png 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gpt-image-1)\">AI<\/span><\/figure><\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What an ERV does that open windows can&#039;t<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">An energy recovery ventilator is a small cabinet \u2014 attic or basement mounted, about the size of a carry-on suitcase \u2014 with two fans and a heat-exchange core. One fan pushes stale indoor air out; the other draws fresh outdoor air in; the core lets the two streams trade heat and moisture without mixing. In winter, incoming air arrives already warmed by seventy to eighty percent of the temperature difference.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The moisture transfer is why an ERV, not its heat-only cousin the HRV, is the usual choice in Bethlehem&#039;s mixed-humid climate. On a muggy July day the core hands part of the incoming air&#039;s moisture back to the outgoing stream, so your air conditioning is not asked to wring out every cubic foot of ventilation air.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In winter the transfer runs the other way, keeping a tight house from drying to static-shock levels while exhausting stale air. The quantities are smaller than people imagine. Standard sizing works out to roughly sixty to ninety cubic feet per minute for a typical three-bedroom house \u2014 a gentle, silent trickle, not a gale. Fan power draw is comparable to a couple of LED fixtures. The point is not volume;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">it is that the exchange happens every hour of every day, regardless of wind and weather.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large alignwide\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-filter-1-1024x683.png\" alt=\"filter - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1487\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-filter-1-1024x683.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-filter-1-300x200.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-filter-1-768x512.png 768w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-filter-1.png 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gpt-image-1)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--ink has-contrast-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--sand has-tint-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The ventilation system that fits your house<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide s-feature-row is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-794e3cfa wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b.jpg\" alt=\"hvac technician repair\" class=\"wp-image-188\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b-300x225.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b-768x576.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;AC Service&quot; by SuperTech HVAC Services, BY-SA, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Blower-door testing<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Establish how tight your house actually is. Baseline ACH50 determines whether mechanical ventilation is needed.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-1024x683.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1475\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-1024x683.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-300x200.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-768x512.png 768w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1.png 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gpt-image-1)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">ERV sizing &amp; routing<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Dedicated small-diameter ducts thread through closets and floor cavities. Fresh air supplies to bedrooms; exhaust from kitchens and baths.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-1024x683.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1476\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-1024x683.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-300x200.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-768x512.png 768w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2.png 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gpt-image-1)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Media filtration<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Four-inch pleated filters deliver MERV 11-13 with low resistance. Changes twice yearly instead of monthly.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/Ductless_Mini_Split_Heat_Pump_Installation.jpg\" alt=\"mini split heat pump\" class=\"wp-image-202\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/Ductless_Mini_Split_Heat_Pump_Installation.jpg 800w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/Ductless_Mini_Split_Heat_Pump_Installation-300x225.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/Ductless_Mini_Split_Heat_Pump_Installation-768x576.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;Ductless Mini Split Heat Pump Installation&quot; by Vernon Air Con, BY-SA, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Return-duct sealing<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Leaky returns pull cellar air straight into supply, bypassing filters. Sealed returns protect the entire system.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1755\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Combustion safety check<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Radiator-heated homes with atmospherically vented boilers need depressurization safeguards. Balanced ventilation prevents back-drafting.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-minisplit-1-1024x683.png\" alt=\"minisplit - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1481\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-minisplit-1-1024x683.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-minisplit-1-300x200.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-minisplit-1-768x512.png 768w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-minisplit-1.png 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gpt-image-1)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Carbon dioxide &amp; humidity logging<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Multi-day readings from occupied rooms show the actual fresh-air deficit before equipment selection.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--cream has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text\" style=\"grid-template-columns:50% auto\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1756\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">From Moravian stone to South Side rows<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Northampton County&#039;s oldest housing concentrates the ventilation problem in different ways. The colonial-era stone buildings of the Moravian district along the Monocacy Creek have massive walls that buffer temperature swings but hold moisture stubbornly once it gets in. The brick rowhomes built on the South Side during the steel era share party walls, so when exposed faces get sealed, total leakage drops fast and indoor air quality turns quickly.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The thick-wall Moravian homes along Main Street were built tight, and modern weatherization makes them tighter still. When PPL bills drop but indoor air turns stale by February, that is the signal. An ERV pulls in lake-wind fresh air without losing your heat, and the sizing matters because a too-small unit will not keep up when you have a full house in January.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The South Side rowhomes between Third and Fourth streets are the tightest we test \u2014 spray foam under shared rooflines drops ACH50 below 2.0, which is too tight without mechanical ventilation. North of the Lehigh, the colonials along Center Street have balloon framing that leaks enough to stay habitable but not enough to stay comfortable. Each block has its own air-sealing story, and the ventilation prescription follows from the blower-door number.<\/p>\n\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-diagnostic has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-b267b866 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:3rem;padding-right:3rem;padding-bottom:3rem;padding-left:3rem\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Sealed-home ventilation indicators<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Bathroom exhaust fan pulls front door inward \u2014 house is tight enough to need balanced ventilation<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Cooking odors linger for hours \u2014 inadequate fresh air dilution in the kitchen zone<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Windows fog on the inside during winter \u2014 excess moisture trapped without exhaust pathway<\/li>\n\n\n<li>CO2 readings above 1000 ppm in occupied rooms \u2014 insufficient outdoor air exchange per occupant<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Stuffy feeling despite comfortable temperature \u2014 low fresh air rate per person per hour<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Radon retest higher after air-sealing than before \u2014 negative pressure pulling soil gas through foundation<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--warm-gradient has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Moisture, infiltration, and the pressure balance<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-indent has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Moisture follows the same logic as air leakage. A household of four releases roughly two to three gallons of water vapor a day through cooking, showering, laundry, and breathing. That vapor used to ride the leaks out of the building. Now it accumulates until it finds the coldest surface available: single-pane glass behind a storm window, the uninsulated corner of a stone wall, the back of a closet.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Window condensation is the visible symptom; condensation inside a wall assembly is the expensive one. The tempting shortcut \u2014 run the bath fans more \u2014 helps less than expected and carries a risk specific to older housing. Exhaust-only ventilation depressurizes the house, and many radiator-heated homes still have an atmospherically vented boiler whose flue depends on gentle upward buoyancy.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sustained negative pressure can pull combustion gases backward down that flue, and it also draws more soil gas, including radon, through the basement floor. Balanced ventilation, where air in equals air out, sidesteps both problems.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">What Bethlehem owners ask about ERVs and air quality<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-accordion s-accordion--bordered has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-1583283a wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>I run my bathroom fans and a kitchen hood. Isn&#039;t that ventilation?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It is spot exhaust, and it stays valuable \u2014 moisture and cooking byproducts should be removed at the source. But it runs only intermittently, supplies no filtered replacement air, and pulls the house negative while operating. An ERV works continuously and in balance. The two are complements, not substitutes.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>Will running a ventilator around the clock undo my insulation savings?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The recovery core returns most of the heat in the outgoing air to the incoming stream, so the energy cost of ERV ventilation is a small fraction of what the same airflow cost when it arrived as uncontrolled leakage. A tight house with an ERV uses meaningfully less energy than the leaky house did \u2014 and has better air.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>My basement is damp all summer. Is an ERV the fix or do I need a dehumidifier?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They do different jobs. An ERV exchanges air and moderates the moisture it brings in; it does not actively dry the house. If summer readings show sustained high humidity, a dedicated dehumidifier handles that directly. A week of logged humidity data settles which problem you actually have before money moves.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>Can an ERV retrofit into a radiator-heated house without ductwork?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Yes. A dedicated ERV system uses small-diameter ducts \u2014 typically three to four inches \u2014 that thread through closets, pantries, and floor cavities far more easily than heating trunk ever could. Fresh air supplies land in bedrooms and living spaces; exhaust pulls from kitchens and baths. The exterior terminations are modest hoods painted to match, well away from the streetscape.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list s-pills s-pills--glass\">\n<li>Blower-door test target: 3\u20135 ACH50 for sealed homes<\/li>\n\n\n<li>ERV recovery rate: 70\u201380% of outgoing heat<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Fresh air volume: 60\u201390 CFM continuous<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Media filter change: twice yearly<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Typical installation: $3,000\u2013$5,000<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Moravian district: vapor-open insulation required<\/li>\n\n\n<li>South Side rows: spray foam under roof<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Combustion safety: critical for radiator homes<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-nearby has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Also serving nearby:<\/strong> <a href=\"\/six-things-to-know-before-switching-your-allentown-home-to-a-heat-pump\/\">Allentown<\/a> \u00b7 <a href=\"\/cut-summer-cooling-costs-in-reading-without-giving-up-comfort\/\">Reading<\/a><\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">Our Work in Your Neighborhood<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery alignwide has-nested-images columns-3 is-cropped s-gallery wp-block-gallery-2 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\">\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" data-id=\"188\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b.jpg\" alt=\"hvac technician repair\" class=\"wp-image-188\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b-300x225.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b-768x576.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;AC Service&quot; by SuperTech HVAC Services, BY-SA, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=